{{main|Aircraft in fiction#B-52 Stratofortress|l1 = Aircraft in fiction, B-52 Stratofortress}}

A B-52 carrying nuclear weapons was a key part of [[Stanley Kubrick]]'s 1964 black comedy film ''[[Dr. Strangelove|Dr. Strangelove or: How I Learned to Stop Worrying and Love the Bomb]]''.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.filmmakermagazine.com/fall2004/line_items/strangelove.php |title=Checkup with Dr. Strangelove |last=Southern |first=Terry |author-link=Terry Southern |year=2009 |access-date=11 January 2010 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20100201221121/http://filmmakermagazine.com/fall2004/line_items/strangelove.php |archive-date=1 February 2010 |url-status=live}}</ref> A 1960s hairstyle, the [[Beehive (hairstyle)|beehive]], is also called a B-52 for its resemblance to the aircraft's distinctive nose.<ref name=Beehive>{{cite news |last1=Weber |first1=Bruce |title=Why We Celebrated the Beehive and Its Maker |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2016/06/15/insider/why-we-celebrated-the-beehive-and-its-maker.html |work=The New York Times |date=15 June 2016}}</ref> The popular band [[the B-52s]] was subsequently named after this hairstyle.<ref name=Beehive/><ref>{{cite news |url=http://www.cnn.com/2007/LIVING/homestyle/07/20/bad.hair/index.html |title=A history of bad hairstyles |publisher=CNN |date=20 July 2007 |first1=Ransom |last1=Riggs}}</ref>It appears in the 2010 [[first-person shooter]] game [[Call of Duty: Black Ops|Call of Duty: Black Ops 1]] in the campaign and in the multiplayer as the "Rolling Thunder" killstreak that performs a [[Carpet bombing|carpet bomb]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Philip |first=Rohan |title=Greatest Killstreaks In Call of Duty {{!}} Page 33 |url=https://gamingbolt.com/greatest-killstreaks-in-call-of-duty/33 |access-date=1 April 2026 |website=GamingBolt |language=en-US}}</ref> The B-52 was added to [[War Thunder]] as a reward for completing stages in the 2026 [[April Fools' Day|April fools]] "Nuclear Thunder" limited time event.{{importance inline|date=April 2026}}<ref>{{cite web |title=Nuclear Thunder! |url=https://warthunder.com/en/news/9983-event-nuclear-thunder-en |website=War Thunder |publisher=Gaijin |access-date=15 April 2026}}</ref>

